Adapt the roles to the actual application.

IMPORTANT:

Never rely only on frontend route protection.

Every sensitive operation must be authorized on the server/backend.

Examples:

A normal user must NOT be able to:

- Access another user's financial information
- Modify another user's application
- Approve their own financial request
- Modify administrative records
- Change transaction status
- Access admin APIs
- Download unauthorized documents
- Modify payment information

Use a **deny-by-default authorization model**.

